svg.metadata:
sibling-of: works/everline-components-master.svg (2026-07-19), works/everline-components-batch2.svg (2026-07-20) — independent batch, not a supersession of either;
spec-reference: docs/design-system-v0.1-batch3-draft.md (updated for each component after its candidate is reviewed);
status: components 1-2/8 (Progress/Spinner/Loading, Search field) are both reviewed and graduated — their SVG groups (c-progress-spinner-loading, c-search-field) are frozen historical snapshots and must not be updated further; superseded-by: works/html/batch3/index.html (candidate spec authority for components 1-2/8 only, not the rest of this file). This file as a whole is NOT retired — unlike everline-components-batch2.svg (fully superseded once all 7 of its components graduated), batch 3 is drawn incrementally one issue at a time, so this sheet stays the active drawing surface for the not-yet-graduated components 3-8/8; created: 2026-07-27; do-not-treat-as-frozen applies only to components 3-8/8, not yet drawn;
scope: batch 3 (8 components) is drawn incrementally, one GitHub issue at a time; this file now holds components 1-2/8 — Progress / Spinner / Loading (issue #5, graduated, frozen snapshot) and Search field (issue #6, graduated, frozen snapshot). Components 3-8 (issues #7-#12) will still be appended to this same file as each is worked — graduating a component freezes only that component's own SVG group, not the whole sheet. This is the first Everline sheet to mix frozen (graduated) and active (not-yet-drawn) groups in one file — everline-components-master.svg has no graduated components yet (per AGENTS.md, batch 1 isn't required to graduate to HTML/CSS until a component is specifically picked), so it isn't a precedent for this per-group-freeze pattern, only for the general "sheet accumulates components across sessions" structure;
backfill-note: issue #5 also requires the progress/spinner component to backfill the `loading` state left deliberately unimplemented for List, Data table and Kanban column (see docs/design-system-v0.1-batch2-draft.md 跨元件設計決策, GitHub issue #13). Already completed in works/html/batch2/, unrelated to Search field;
token-gap: component.progress.*/component.spinner.* were added to tokens/everline-draft.tokens.json after issue #5's candidate was approved. Search field (issue #6) is designed to need only one new group, component.search-field.*, and only for icon/clear-button layout metrics — every color and the field height/radius/background reuse component.text-input's existing values directly (see search-field-note below and 校準清單 under the Search field group). New tokens are proposed only after this candidate is approved, per AGENTS.md's token-before-use rule;
search-field-note: Search field (issue #6) deliberately extends component.text-input's structure (48px height, radius.control, background-subdued, gray-700 placeholder/icon tone, border-focus) instead of inventing a parallel token namespace, per the issue's own scope note ("延伸既有 Text input 的 token 與結構"). Scope is intentionally narrow (低複雜度): only empty/filled/focused/disabled states plus a leading search icon and a content-conditional trailing clear button — no error/readonly variant, since those aren't typical for a search field and Text input itself only specifies them as future work.
